 use and development of mobile applications and cashless payment systems over the period from 2017 to 2021. This market study involves the creation of specific indicators designed to measure and compare the utilization of mobile applications against other forms of cashless payment systems. By focusing on these aspects, the analysis provides insights into the trends and shifts in consumer behavior regarding mobile banking and cashless transactions within Poland during this timeframe. The study aims to offer a comprehensive understanding of how mobile banking applications are being adopted and how they stack up against other cashless payment methods, reflecting the evolving landscape of financial technology in Poland.", "HCE CARDS:", "INTERNET BANKING:", "COVID-19 PANDEMIC:The COVID-19 pandemic, a global health crisis that began in 2020, had far-reaching impacts on various aspects of life worldwide, including significant changes in consumer behavior and payment trends. In Poland, the pandemic led to the declaration of a state of epidemic, prompting administrative changes across retail and service sectors. These changes included the imposition of restrictions and a strong promotion of cashless payments to minimize physical contact and curb the spread of the virus.\n\nAs a result, there was a notable shift towards cashless transactions, with a marked increase in the use of online and mobile banking services. This shift was particularly evident among older generations, who traditionally relied more on cash but began adopting digital payment methods during the pandemic. The popularity of online shopping surged as physical trade faced restrictions, further driving the demand for payment cards and digital payment systems.\n\nOne of the significant outcomes of this shift was the increased usage of BLIK, a mobile payment system, especially among the oldest consumer group. The pandemic acted as a catalyst for the adoption of such technologies, as consumers sought safer and more convenient ways to conduct transactions without physical interaction.\n\nOverall, the COVID-19 pandemic not only altered consumer behavior but also accelerated the digital transformation of payment systems, highlighting the importance of adaptability in the face of unprecedented global challenges.", "TRADITIONAL PAYMENT CARDS:Traditional payment cards were the most popular form of payment during the pandemic, although their demand was affected by the rise of online shopping and the introduction of contactless systems like BLIK", "ING:ING is a prominent bank in Poland, recognized for its advanced mobile banking services. The bank provides a variety of secure mobile banking login methods, including PIN, fingerprint, and face scan, ensuring a convenient and safe user experience. ING's mobile banking platform is widely utilized, boasting 2.25 million active mobile app users. This significant user base is part of a larger clientele, with ING serving 4.35 million individual clients across Poland. The bank's mobile application usage metrics have been a subject of analysis, highlighting its importance and effectiveness in the digital banking landscape. ING's commitment to integrating cutting-edge technology into its services underscores its role as a leader in the Polish banking sector.", "PEKAO:PEKAO is one of the major banks in Poland, recognized for its comprehensive mobile banking services. As a prominent financial institution, PEKAO has been at the forefront of integrating advanced technology into its banking operations, providing customers with a variety of convenient mobile banking login methods. These include the use of a PIN, fingerprint recognition, and face scan, ensuring both security and ease of access for its users.\n\nSince 2018, PEKAO has also been offering BLIK services, a popular mobile payment system in Poland, further enhancing its digital banking capabilities. This service allows customers to make quick and secure transactions using their mobile devices, reflecting the bank's commitment to innovation and customer convenience.\n\nPEKAO's mobile application has been a subject of analysis for its usage metrics, indicating a focus on understanding and improving user engagement and satisfaction. As part of a group with moderate mobile banking indicators, PEKAO continues to strive for excellence in its digital offerings, aiming to meet the evolving needs of its clientele.\n\nOverall, PEKAO stands out as a key player in the Polish banking sector, leveraging technology to provide efficient and secure banking solutions to its customers.", "SANTANDER:Santander is a prominent financial institution operating in Poland, known for its comprehensive range of mobile banking services and functionalities. The bank has been a key player in the Polish banking sector, particularly noted for its innovative approach to mobile banking. Santander offers a variety of secure mobile banking login methods to enhance user convenience and security. These methods include traditional password entry, masked passwords, PIN codes, as well as biometric options such as fingerprint and face scan recognition, catering to a wide array of customer preferences and ensuring robust security measures.\n\nSince 2015, Santander has been providing BLIK services, a popular mobile payment system in Poland that allows users to make instant payments using their mobile devices. This service has been integral to Santander's mobile banking offerings, reflecting the bank's commitment to adopting cutting-edge technologies to meet the evolving needs of its customers.\n\nThe bank's mobile application is a focal point of its digital strategy, and it has been subject to analysis for its usage metrics, indicating a strong emphasis on understanding and improving customer engagement and satisfaction. Through its mobile app, Santander provides a seamless banking experience, enabling customers to perform a wide range of banking activities conveniently from their smartphones.\n\nOverall, Santander in Poland stands out for its dedication to providing advanced mobile banking solutions, ensuring both security and ease of use for its customers. The bank's continuous efforts to innovate and adapt to the digital landscape underscore its position as a leader in the Polish banking industry.", "MILLENNIUM:Millennium is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized for its leadership in mobile banking services. As part of a leading group in the mobile banking sector, Millennium has been at the forefront of integrating advanced technology into its banking solutions. The bank offers a variety of mobile banking login methods, including the use of a PIN and fingerprint recognition, ensuring secure and convenient access for its customers. Since 2015, Millennium has also been providing BLIK services, a popular mobile payment system in Poland, further enhancing its digital banking offerings. The bank's mobile application usage metrics have been a subject of analysis, highlighting its commitment to understanding and improving customer experience in the digital realm. Through these innovative services, Millennium continues to solidify its position as a key player in Poland's banking industry.", "ALIOR:Alior is a bank in Poland, analyzed for its mobile application usage metrics", "POCZTOWY:Pocztowy is a bank in Poland, analyzed for its mobile application usage metrics", "WARD'S METHOD:Ward's method is a clustering analysis technique used to identify similarities and differences among banks in mobile application usage", "PKO PB:PKO PB is one of the four banks in Group 3, characterized by an average level of mobile banking adoption among its customers", "MINISTRY OF DEVELOPMENT:The Ministry of Development issued recommendations to limit COVID-19 transmission in retail outlets", "VISA:Visa increased the contactless transaction limit to reduce the need for PIN entry during the COVID-19 pandemic", "MASTERCARD:Mastercard is a global payment technology company that has been proactive in adapting to the evolving needs of its users, particularly during the COVID-19 pandemic. In response to the increased demand for safer and more convenient payment methods, Mastercard increased the contactless transaction limit. This strategic move was aimed at reducing the need for PIN entry, thereby minimizing physical contact and enhancing the safety and convenience of transactions during the pandemic.\n\nIn addition to its efforts to improve transaction safety, Mastercard has also been active in expanding its technological capabilities through strategic partnerships. In 2019, Mastercard partnered with PSP to enhance BLIK's contactless payment capabilities. This collaboration was part of Mastercard's broader strategy to innovate and improve the efficiency and reach of its payment solutions, ensuring that users have access to seamless and advanced payment technologies.\n\nThrough these initiatives, Mastercard has demonstrated its commitment to providing secure, efficient, and innovative payment solutions on a global scale."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_dbe34a2c0a0e265c41f75f374af3a8830a7b56399d0cc5eccb919ef92b658b62_v2"}